 <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Vertex of a Parabola</title>
            
<p component="b" workspace="4in">
    Now that we know how to convert between these forms, we can use that to help us analyze a quadratic function, potentially without changing the form.
</p>
<p component="a">
    Now that we know how to convert between these forms, we can use that to help us analyze a quadratic function, potentially without changing the form. Finding the vertex, know if max or min.
</p>

        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
            Therefore, for the quadratic <m>f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c</m>, the vertex is
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            Therefore, for the quadratic <m>f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c</m> , the vertex is at the <m>x</m>-coordinate <m>-\frac{b}{2a}</m>...
        </p>

        <example workspace="2in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    Find the vertex of the parabola <md>
                        f(x) = 3x^2 - 7x + 13
                    </md>. Is this point a maximum or a minimum for the parabola?
                    
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <paragraphs>
            <title>Applications</title>
            
            <p component="b" workspace="4in">
                How can we use this for applications?
            </p>
            <p component="a">
                How can we use this for applications? If we have a word problem with a quadratic, we can now ask what the max or min value is.
            </p>
        </paragraphs>
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="0in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Assume that the average ticket price for a sporting event is given by 
                    <md>
                        p(t) = -\frac{5}{8}t^2 + \frac{35}{4}t + 100
                    </md>, where <m>p</m> is in dollars and <m>t</m> is the number of weeks after the start of the season. 
                    
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Does the ticket price have a maximum or minimum value?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        What is that value and where does it achieve it?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>

    <page>
        <example workspace="4in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    A vegetable garden has been built alongside a solid wooden fence. This garden is built with <quantity><mag>16</mag><unit base="foot"/></quantity> of wire fencing on the three additional sides (excluding the wooden fence). What dimensions of the garden maximize its area?
                </p>
            </statement>
        
        </example>
        
    </page>


<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Rational Equations and Functions</title>
        
<p component="b" workspace="4in">
    The next class of functions that we want to deal with are rational functions.
</p>
<p component="a">
    The next class of functions that we want to deal with are rational functions. Rational means ratio, or including fractions. Write an example. How do we solve these? We clear all denominators and then solve it normally.
</p>

    </paragraphs>
</page>

<page>
    <example workspace="4in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve <md>
                    \frac{2}{x} = x + 1
                </md>.
                
            </p>
        </statement>
    
    </example>
    
</page>

<page>
    <example workspace="4in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve <md>
                    \frac{3}{x+5} = \frac{1}{2x-1}
                </md>.
                
            </p>
        </statement>
    
    </example>
    
</page>

<page>
    <p>
        It's also important to check your answers to these problems to make sure they work in the original equation. For rational functions, there's a chance that you get an <term>extraneous</term> solution when you clear denominators.
    </p>

    <example workspace="4in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Solve <md>
                    \frac{2x-5}{x-2} = \frac{x+1}{x+2} + \frac{2x}{x^2 - 4}
                </md>.
                
            </p>
        </statement>
    
    </example>
    
</page>

<page>
    <paragraphs>
        <title>Rational Expressions and Functions</title>

        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
            What if we have a rational function, something that looks like <md>
                f(x) = \frac{3}{x+2} - \frac{5x+1}{x-3}
            </md>. What can we do with that?  
            
        </p>
        <p component="a">
            What if we have a rational function, something that looks like <md>
                f(x) = \frac{3}{x+2} - \frac{5x+1}{x-3}
            </md>. What can we do with that? Need to get to a common denominator and leave that on the bottom. We don't have another side of the equation to clear things to. 
             
        </p>


        
    </paragraphs>
</page>

<page>
    <example workspace="4in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Write <md>
                    f(x) = \frac{x-\frac{5}{2}}{x-6} + \frac{x - \frac{1}{2}}{x-2}
                </md> as a single fraction. Then, use this to determine the values of <m>x</m> where <m>f(x) = 1</m>.
                
            </p>
        </statement>
    
    </example>
    
</page>

